## Summary

I implemented **`ChargingListPage`** — a native SwiftUI/Apple-HIG parity port of the web `web/src/features/charging/pages/ChargingListPage.tsx` (route `/charging`), adaptive across macOS + iOS — and committed it (`21b16867`).

**What shipped** (13 source files + 1 test under `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Charging/` — the real build-compiled path, documented in the log):
- **6 KPI panels** (Sessions, Energy-kWh, Cost, Avg-rate-kW, Avg-duration, Avg-power-kW) with prior-period deltas + the no-stats **GlassPanel7**, bound from an `@Observable` model.
- **MetricSwitcher trend chart** via the P3 Swift Charts wrappers (bars for sessions/energy/cost, line for avg power).
- Sticky summary, search + active-filter chips, collection pills, secondary breakdown line, anomaly callout, list controls (sort/density), **bulk-delete toolbar with confirm**, date-grouped rows, pagination, and threshold-gated analytical sections (AC/DC, battery-dist, efficiency, specs, optimizer).
- All four data states (loading/empty/error/success) for every source; SI Wh/W converted only at the render boundary; 67 web i18n keys ported verbatim into `Localizable.xcstrings`.
- Data-source seam mapping the three web hooks (`useChargingSessionsPaginated`, `useChargingOptimizer`, `useBulkDeleteCharging`).

